#: ../../source/docs/archived-apm2x-wiring-quickstart.rst:205
#: 07c0b63570294c10bdafd722fcafb6f6
msgid "Installing it in your plane"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/archived-apm2x-wiring-quickstart.rst:207
#: 7cfbfe2640bd43f78ed043d060412957
msgid "When you place APM in your aircraft, it is very important that it face the right way. The GPS connector should face forward, and the servo cables face back. The board must also be right side up, with the IMU shield at the top. Like this (note: there's a little arrow on the bottom of the shield that point to the front, too, in case you need a reminder at the field):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/archived-apm2x-wiring-quickstart.rst:217
#: 3462234ac5d94753b5b5eecc6b6c504a
msgid "When putting APM in your plane, it's important to ensure that it's solidly mounted and doesn't move around in flight. It should also be as close as possible to level when the plane is in its flying orientation. Ideally, you'll want to have it as close to the center of gravity as you can (that's where vibration is the least) and mounted on foam tape onto a solid platform."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/archived-apm2x-wiring-quickstart.rst:225
#: acce1136e8cc4b2cabeec20fc538705b
msgid "Connecting GPS Module"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/archived-apm2x-wiring-quickstart.rst:227
#: d2c3746b40214f33a03759c659f5af74
msgid "A GPS module provides enhanced positioning for autonomous flight. Connecting your GPS to your autopilot by following these steps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/archived-apm2x-wiring-quickstart.rst:231
#: 4a709b857b2342d8beb5bbc76eb4f238
msgid "3DR GPS uBlox with Onboard Compass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/archived-apm2x-wiring-quickstart.rst:233
#: 2e358b4b7e1147afae2300833aff421a
msgid "3DR GPS uBlox with Onboard Compass is intended for use with APM 2.5 (for external compass). It provides enhanced compass performance because of the freedom to situate the GPS unit in an optimal position independent of the location of the APM. Place your GPS on the outside of your plane with a clear view of the sky, as far as possible from the motor and ESC, with the arrow facing forward."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/archived-apm2x-wiring-quickstart.rst:243
#: 4c784a23c4d240e7aa1c54f38915c50c
msgid "Connect the GPS module to the APM 2.6 using the two cables included with the GPS as shown below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/archived-apm2x-wiring-quickstart.rst:249
#: 0053eba9bc0446dea9318caf150c1fe0
msgid "3DR GPS uBlox with Onboard Compass includes two connector cables: one 4-position cable and one 5-position-to-6-position cable. To connect the GPS module to APM 2.6, connect the GPS to the APM GPS port using the 5-position-to-6-position cable; connect the GPS to the APM I2C port using the 4-position cable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/archived-apm2x-wiring-quickstart.rst:256
#: db4cc92638624e6d8ed06182def1d339
msgid "3DR GPS uBlox without Onboard Compass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/archived-apm2x-wiring-quickstart.rst:258
#: 85cb7c79a9dd4f38bd807fc9a36bad28
msgid "3DR GPS uBlox without Onboard Compass is intended for use with APM 2.5. To install your GPS module without compass, mount to the outside of your plane with a clear view of the sky and connect to the APM 2.5 GPS port using the 5-position-to-6-position connector cable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/archived-apm2x-wiring-quickstart.rst:267
#: 13cc367913444af79bfd76474dcf2dec
msgid "Tips on mounting the GPS module"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/archived-apm2x-wiring-quickstart.rst:269
#: ad226ce4147d499da64d6516fe335364
msgid "It doesn't matter which way the GPS module is oriented, as long as the square antenna side is facing up"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/archived-apm2x-wiring-quickstart.rst:271
#: 9c181eba33d04d129bdf6114dd412da3
msgid "It's best to mount the GPS as far away from radio transmission equipment (like your telemetry or video transmitters) as possible."
